    {
      "items": [
        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "As a Developer, I want a reusable wishlist/login-panel React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it renders as a slide-in panel from the right when a logged-out shopper attempts to add an item to their wishlist.\n\nThe panel presents authentication options to the shopper so they can log in or create an account before their wishlist action is completed. It does not own the wishlist icon trigger — that is handled by pdp/product-content. Authentication logic and API integration are covered in the relevant auth functional stories.\n\nOpen items:\n\n@Kiera — this component is not yet componentized in the Design System Figma. The design exists in the PDP drawers section (node 40001369-36097). Please extract into a named component before dev picks this up.",
          "to_string": "As a Developer, I want a {{wishlist-login-panel}} content component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it renders the authentication prompt inside the {{pdp/drawer}} (SFCC-736) when a logged-out shopper attempts to add an item to their wishlist.\n\nThe component covers the panel content only — the drawer shell, slide-in behaviour, overlay, and close trigger are owned by {{pdp/drawer}} (SFCC-736). This component renders as children passed into that shell.\n\nThe panel content comprises three sections separated by dividers:\n\n# Email / OTP section — explanatory copy, email input field, and Send Code CTA\n# Social sign-in section — Sign in with Apple and Sign in with Google buttons\n# New account section — New to Zimmermann? heading, supporting copy, and Create an Account CTA\n\nAuthentication logic and API integration are out of scope for this story and are covered in the relevant auth stories.\n\n||Prop|| ||Values|| ||Notes||\n|size|Large, Small, Mobile|Controls layout variant|"
        }
      ],
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-21T14:49:17.917000+10:00"
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "wishlist/login-panel",
          "to_string": "Wishlist – Login Panel Content"
        },
        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "Panel shell\n\n1. Given a logged-out shopper clicks the wishlist icon, then the panel slides in from the right as defined in the design system.\n2. Given the panel is open, then a close icon is visible in the header and closes the panel on click.\n\nContent\n\n3. Given the panel renders, then it displays the WISHLIST heading and instructional text explaining that the shopper must log in or create an account to save items.\n4. Given the panel renders, then an email Textfield atom and a SEND CODE button are visible for magic link / OTP login.\n5. Given the panel renders, then a Sign in with Apple button is visible.\n6. Given the panel renders, then a Sign in with Google button is visible.\n7. Given the panel renders, then a NEW TO ZIMMERMANN? section is visible with promotional copy and a CREATE AN ACCOUNT button.\n\nEmpty & error states\n\n8. Given the panel fails to load, then no broken layout is shown.\n\nAccessibility\n\n9. Given the panel opens, then focus moves into the panel and is trapped within it until closed.\n10. Given the panel closes, then focus returns to the wishlist icon that triggered it.\n11. The panel has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n12. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA.",
          "to_string": "Panel behaviour\n\n1. Given a logged-out shopper triggers the wishlist action, when the wishlist icon is clicked, then the panel slides in from the right using the pdp/drawer shell (SFCC-736).\n2. Given the panel is open, when the close icon is clicked, then the panel dismisses and focus returns to the wishlist icon that triggered it.\n\nContent\n\n3. Given the panel renders, then it displays a heading and explanatory copy informing the shopper they must log in or create an account to save items.\n4. Given the panel renders, then an email input field and a \"Send Code\" button are visible for magic link / OTP login.\n5. Given the panel renders, then \"Sign in with Apple\" and \"Sign in with Google\" buttons are visible.\n6. Given the panel renders, then a \"New to Zimmermann?\" section is visible with supporting copy and a \"Create an Account\" CTA.\n\nResponsive\n\n7. Given the component is rendered at size=Large, size=Small, or size=Mobile, when it mounts, then the layout matches the corresponding Figma design spec variant.\n\nEmpty & error states\n\n8. Given the panel content fails to load, then no broken layout is shown and the drawer shell remains dismissible.\n\nAccessibility\n\n9. Given the panel opens, then focus moves into the panel and is trapped within it until closed.\n10. Given the panel closes, then focus returns to the wishlist icon that triggered it.\n11. The panel has role=dialog and an appropriate aria-label.\n12. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA.",
          "from_id": "",
          "to_id": ""
        }
      ],
